90
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
The Hashira!

91
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
I ended up giving him the key so he took off.

92
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
So you gave it to him.

93
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
I guess you didn't have a choice.

94
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Well, since I don't know what's going on, I shouldn't be making a fuss.

95
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
No, it's okay.

96
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
I'm happy.

97
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
You don't know me, but you stood up for me.

98
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Thank you very much.

99
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
I'm sorry I wasn't able to help much.

100
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Wait, what happened to that man?

101
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Where'd he go?

102
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Oh, that was a mechanical doll.

103
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Mechanical doll?

104
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Yeah, and that guy took it away with him.

105
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:17,000
You see, he needed the key in order to make the doll move.

106
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
So that's why it was important.

107
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
But why does he want that doll?

108
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Because it's very special.

109
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Not only can that mechanical doll overpower a human,

110
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
but it's capable of 108 different moves.

111
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
It's often used for combat training.

112
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
So that's why.

113
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
But now it's...

114
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
What was that?

115
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Don't tell me he's already... this way!

116
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Against the Hashira. Amazing.

117
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Isn't it?

118
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
It's the battle type mechanical doll built by my ancestors.

119
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The Yorichi Type Zero.

120
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
But...

121
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Why does he have six arms?

122
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Oh, his arms?

123
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
I asked the same thing.

124
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
According to my father,

125
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,000
that mechanical doll was modeled after an actual swordsman.

126
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
And the only way they could manage to replicate the swordsman's moves

127
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
was by giving it six arms.

128
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
That face...

129
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
It seems familiar.

130
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
But why?

131
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,000
About that swordsman...

132
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Who exactly was he?

133
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Uh...

134
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Sorry, but I don't really know much about him.

135
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
He was from the Sengoku period.

136
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
S...

137
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Sengoku?

138
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
You mean he lived more than 300 years ago?

139
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
That's what I was told.

140
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
In all that time, it's never broken down?

141
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Incredible.

142
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
The technology's so advanced,

143
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
we're still not able to catch up to it.

144
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
So if it were to break,

145
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
there'd be no fixing it.

146
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
My father suddenly passed away,

147
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
and I have no siblings.

148
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
I'm the only one who can step up now.

149
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
But I'm no good with swords or dolls.

150
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
So that's why you...

151
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I think I get it now.

152
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Wow.

153
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
He's incredible.

154
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Even though we're around the same age.

155
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
He's talented.

156
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
And a Hashira.

157
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
And a Hashira.

158
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Well, duh!

159
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
What did you expect?

160
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I mean, he is a descendant of sun breathing users after all.

161
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
That boy is a prodigy, you know.

162
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
He's in a different league than the likes of you.

163
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Ha ha ha ha ha!

164
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Are you Tokito's crow?

165
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Wait, sun breathing?

166
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
The first breathing style?

167
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
So he really is that amazing.

168
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:52,000
But that isn't sun breathing, right?

169
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
If you don't quit your yapping,

170
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
I'm gonna catch your eyes out!

171
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Hey, now I remember.

172
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
My dream.

173
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Yeah, I saw that man in my dream.

174
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Huh?

175
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Are you an idiot or something?

176
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Isn't this your first time here too?

177
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
You sure know how to make me laugh,

178
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
I'll give you that.

179
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
You met a warrior from the Sengoku period?

180
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
How old are you exactly?

181
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Huh?

182
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Listen, I'm sorry.

183
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
I...

184
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
I must be crazy.

185
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
No!

186
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
No!

187
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
I know.

188
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Maybe it's an inherited memory.

189
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
People talk about those a lot in our village.

190
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
It isn't just your physical form that gets passed on.

191
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Living creatures pass on their memories too.

192
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Huh?

193
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
So what you saw in your dream

194
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
had to have been your ancestors' memories!

195
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
That's preposterous!

196
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Actually preposterous!

197
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
How kind of you.

198
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Thank you.

199
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Ha!

200
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
I'm Tanjiro.

201
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
What's your name?

202
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
My name's Kotetsu.

203
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
You can just do what I always do

204
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
and ignore the mean lady crows!

205
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Hey!

206
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
His armor!

207
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Kotetsu!

208
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Kotetsu!

209
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
I'll find you!

210
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
I've got a good nose!

211
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
I'll find you!

212
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I've got a good nose!

213
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Even if it's a bit out of shape.

214
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
I think he ran off this way...

215
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:16,000
...

216
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:30,300
Kotetsu! Kotetsu! I'll find you! I've got a good nose!

217
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:36,000
Even if it's a bit out of shape. I think he ran off this way.

218
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Kotetsu! How in the world did you manage to climb up that high?

219
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Come on, you can't give up on your doll. I'll do anything I can to help you out.

220
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
What about your future?

221
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:05,000
If you try hard now for your future self, then a day will come where you can fight and stand up for yourself.

222
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:15,000
No, it won't. I'm smart enough to know that I'm a loser, okay? Because of me, it's all gonna end with my generation!

223
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Huh? Ouchie!

224
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:24,000
You cannot give up and walk away from it. I really wish you wouldn't talk about yourself that way.

225
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:29,000
He didn't make a sound! Swordsmen are scary!

226
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Even if you can't do it, there will be someone who will carry on for you. You have to do what you can so it gets passed on. If you fail, maybe your kids or grandkids will succeed.

227
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:53,000
I want to be the one to put an end to Muzan Kibutsu-chi. And to save my sister who's been turned into a demon. I might die before I fulfill my goals.

228
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Huh?

229
00:11:54,000 --> 00:12:09,000
But I have faith that someone will carry out my wishes, the same way we were able to when we beat an upper rank. So I know in my heart that someday, Muzan Kibutsu-chi will fall!

230
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Let's give her all!

231
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:31,000
I… I couldn't stand to watch him break the door. But that was before! The combat training should last until nightfall. I promise I'll see this through! To the end!

232
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Yeah! Really? So you're Tenko Tetsu?

233
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Yeah! My little brother is… Huh? What? You're already done?

234
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:56,000
I'm finished. It made for good training. Do I know you? Oh, that's right. My sword snapped, so…

235
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Huh?

236
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
This will do. For the time being.

237
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Kotetsu!

238
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
There. Now dispose of it.

239
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Not even a whiff of malice. He must not be doing it on purpose. That being said…

240
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:26,000
His crow is oozing with animosity. She's so condescending. What gives?

241
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Oh! Kotetsu!

242
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Kotetsu. Let's make sure. And see if it still works.

243
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Uh…

244
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Nothing… It must be…

245
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Alright! It's working, Kotetsu! That's… great!

246
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Yes it is, Mr. Tanjiro. And do you know why? Because now you can train with this doll and become stronger than that indifferent little jerk! And you'll have my full support, no matter what!

247
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Huh? Wait, right now?

248
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Ahhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh!

249
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Whoaaahhhhhhhhhhhhhh!

250
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Wooooahhhhhh!

251
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
I'm gonna die! Six arms is so many!

252
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:03,000
There are only five arms! Since that lousy jerk broke one off, it's way easier to beat now!

253
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
It's way easier to beat now.

254
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Mr. Tanjiro, please, we need you stronger.

255
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
So next time we see him, you can say,

256
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
That all you got, you scumbag?

257
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:19,000
It's time to get a haircut, seaweed head.

258
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Piss here! Your ugly and your legs are short!

259
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Commit seppuku, you shameless jerk!

260
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,000
No! Mr. Kotetsu! That's going too far!

261
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
You think we should put his head on public display?

262
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
What? No! I'm not saying any of that!

263
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Yes, you are!

264
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
No!

265
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Please say it! Please!

266
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Tokito was incredible. He hardly broke a sweat.

267
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Despite being smaller and younger than me,

268
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:57,000
I have to train harder so that I can become stronger.

269
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Come on, Mr. Tanjiro! Don't tell me that's all it takes to kill you!

270
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Now, come on! Get up! I'm gonna say it one more time! Look at me!

271
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:20,000
All you're doing now is moving out of habit, Mr. Tanjiro!

272
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
You're not reacting off your opponent's moves whatsoever!

273
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
That's why you're getting beat, understand?

274
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Which in other words means you don't even have the fundamentals of sword fighting down yet!

275
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
It's a miracle you haven't died!

276
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Good thing I'm here to expose your weak points until we fix them!

277
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
And to give you some extra motivation, no food until we're finished!

278
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Right...

279
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Faster, Mr. Tanjiro! You gotta pick up the pace!

280
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:57,000
If that doll wasn't armed with practice sticks, you'd be dead! Get it together!

281
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:02,000
We're on day five now, so starting tomorrow, I'm gonna arm the doll with swords!

282
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:07,000
That is... if I even live to see day six, I'm... I'm gonna die!

283
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
No food for you today, either!

284
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Mr. Kotetsu's surprisingly analytical.

285
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
But as a swordsmanship instructor, he was terrible!

286
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
It's like he has no idea what the limits of the human body are.

287
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
And his brutal training reflects that.

288
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:31,000
He's gotten to be so ruthless, that he'll withhold food and water if you fall short.

289
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:35,000
But a human can only go without water for three days or so.

290
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
It's pure tyranny, born out of his ignorance.

291
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Luckily, I was able to survive thanks to rainfall.

292
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:56,000
All throughout these harsh training sessions, I went without water, without food, without sleep.

293
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,000
And then, I started to cross the river to the afterlife.

294
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:14,000
I was walking across a bridge, feeling an indescribable bliss, only to get dizzy from hunger and fall in the river.

295
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:22,000
The water got darker and darker, heavier and heavier, until I felt a strange warmth.

296
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
It was almost like I was being massaged.

297
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:30,000
When I glanced towards the bottom of the river, I saw something shiny.

298
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
So I swam towards it while being massaged.

299
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Oddly enough, despite being underwater, I could smell the shimmering stone.

300
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:45,000
What is this?

301
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
The smell?

302
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
It's different than the opening thread.

303
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Left side of the head!

304
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Neck!

305
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Right side!

306
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Left side!

307
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Right thigh!

308
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Right shoulder!

309
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Now!

310
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Left side!

311
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
There you go!

312
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
You finally got one strike in!

313
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
